    <div class="container content">
      <h2>Perfect for Small-Scale Mining</h2>
      <p>The 50 Ton Gold Wash Plant is one of our best sellers, ideal for prospectors and small mining operations. Despite its compact size, it delivers the same 95-98% recovery rate as our larger models. The ~15' sluice captures fine gold down to 200 mesh while the all-in-one design eliminates the need for separate screens or sluice boxes.</p>
      <h3>Who Is the 50 Ton For?</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Small-scale placer miners processing 50 tons per hour or less</li>
        <li>Prospectors testing new claims before scaling up</li>
        <li>Remote operations where portability is critical</li>
        <li>Operators who want professional-grade recovery without the industrial footprint</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Portability & Setup</h3>
      <p>Weighing significantly less than our larger models, the 50-ton unit can be towed by a standard pickup truck. Setup usually takes 30 minutes or less, meaning you can be processing material the same day it arrives. <a href='/how-it-works/'>Learn more about how our wash plants work</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

    <section class="bg-cream product-faq">
    <div class="container content">
      <h2>50 Ton Wash Plant — Common Questions</h2>
      <h3>How much does a 50 ton gold wash plant cost?</h3>
      <p>Every 50 Ton plant is custom-built to the ground it will run on, so we quote each one rather than publish a single list price. Build time is one to three weeks. What moves the number most is the power package, the feed setup and where it ships to. Our <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-cost-guide/">gold wash plant cost guide</a> walks through each of those, and a quote request comes back with a firm figure.</p>
      <h3>How much water does the 50 Ton need?</h3>
      <p>The 50 Ton runs at 500 GPM. That is the flow through the plant, not the volume you have to haul — most operations <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-water-requirements/">recirculate</a> off a settling pond, so a single water source keeps the plant producing for days. Sizing the pond and pump to your ground is part of the quote.</p>
      <h3>What powers a 50 ton wash plant?</h3>
      <p><a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-power-requirements/">Diesel or electric</a>, configured with the plant. Diesel is the usual choice on remote claims with no line power. Electric makes sense where you already have a generator set or grid supply on site.</p>
      <h3>How fine a gold will the 50 Ton hold?</h3>
      <p>The ~15 feet sluice recovers 95-98% down to 200 mesh. Recovery of very fine and <a href="/blog/fine-gold-recovery/">flour gold</a> depends as much on how the material is fed and how the sluice is run as it does on the plant itself.</p>
      <h3>Can the 50 Ton ship outside the United States?</h3>
      <p>Yes. We build in the USA and ship worldwide, and more than half of our enquiries come from outside the country. Containerisation, documentation and <a href="/blog/shipping-gold-wash-plant-internationally/">duty</a> are worth planning before you order, not after.</p>
      <p>Not sure this is the right size? Compare it against the <a href="/products/100-ton/">100 Ton plant</a>, or read our guide to <a href="/blog/choosing-right-size-gold-wash-plant/">choosing the right size wash plant</a> for your ground.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
